  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1211 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nA cold front moves through the area on Wednesday as a mid-level\nlow pressure system moves in from the northwest. Northwesterly \nwinds will become gusty behind the front by Wednesday afternoon\ngusting near 30 mph. Winds stay elevated through the night into\nThursday morning, but will slowly diminish through the day. \nRain chances have all but disappeared with this frontal passage.\nThis is likely due to the better forcing staying closer to the \nbase of the trough which will traverse through NE MO and keep \nthe rain chances further north. Though, it will bring a cooldown\nfor us with a 10 degree high temperature drop from Wednesday \ninto Thursday. Highs will be in the 50s for the end of the week \ninto the weekend with lows the coldest they've been all season. \nBy Friday night, low temperatures dip into the mid 20s and 30s \nwith the coldest temperatures occurring east of Highway 65. No \nrain chances expected Friday into Saturday as mid-level high \npressure moves into the area. By Sunday, another low-pressure \nsystem moves into the Central Plain region. This system has a \n15% chance of bringing rain to our area. We'll continue to \nmonitor the forecast to see if these rain chances stick around.",
